      \field{abstract}{Kerr-Schild double copy is shown to extend naturally to all free symmetric gauge fields propagating on \$(A)dS\$ in any dimensions. Similarly to the standard lower-spin case, the higher-spin multicopy comes along with the zeroth, single and double copies. The mass-like term of the Fronsdal spin \$s\$ field equations fixed by gauge symmetry and the mass of the zeroth copy both appear to be remarkably fine tuned to fit the multicopy pattern forming a spectrum organized by higher-spin symmetry. On the black hole side this curious observation fills up the list of miraculous properties of the Kerr solution.}
